Kenapa Rel Kereta Pakai Kerikil — pilot "Fakta Nyeleneh", versi Brick Toy

Picture: built and rendered entirely in code (three.js r170). Brick geometry & plastic materials (bricks.js) and the
  scene/lighting approach adapted from the Lemo-Opuscar library's Brick Toy demo, MIT License; post pass core/three/post.js (MIT).
3D props & textures (CC0, Poly Haven): Tea Set 01, Desk Lamp Arm 01, walnut wood textures, "Photo Studio Loft Hall" HDRI.
Font: Fredoka — Copyright 2016 The Fredoka Project Authors, SIL Open Font License 1.1 (shipped in the library's core/fonts).
Narration: ElevenLabs (Eleven v3), voice "depa" from the ElevenLabs Voice Library, generated by the Owner (D:/AI Virtual Office/voice/depa 2.mp3), split per line at silences. Per-word captions timed with whisper.cpp. Earlier VoxCPM2 takes kept in out/vo_v3_final.
Music samples (CC0 1.0): VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition and Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios) —
  contrabass pizzicato, marimba, glockenspiel, xylophone, harp, vibraphone; FreePats project — kalimba.
Synthesised in code: brick clicks, plastic creaks and crashes, gravel pour, rain, train rumble, bell.
No brand names, logos or trademarked figure designs are used; the workers are original figures built from plain bricks.
